1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:03,255
Right now, particles from space are passing through your phone.

2
00:00:03,750 --> 00:00:07,560
About one muon passes through every square centimeter, every minute.

3
00:00:08,050 --> 00:00:12,560
When a particle hits a memory chip just right, it can flip a single bit.

4
00:00:12,560 --> 00:00:13,876
A zero becomes a one.

5
00:00:14,383 --> 00:00:18,291
In 2010, a flipped bit made Voyager 2 send home gibberish,

6
00:00:18,291 --> 00:00:20,447
until engineers flipped it back.

7
00:00:20,950 --> 00:00:22,477
And in Belgium in 2003,

8
00:00:22,477 --> 00:00:30,115
a single flipped bit is the leading explanation for one candidate getting four thousand and ninety-six extra votes.

9
00:00:30,617 --> 00:00:33,155
So why doesn't your computer crash every day?

10
00:00:33,155 --> 00:00:34,622
Full story on the channel.
